/textbook/build/quiz-widget-30a9c49f85f8d76895c10687ac28287f.mjs","model":{"question":"The inspector considers switching from samples of 16 boxes to samples of 64 boxes. How would this change the sampling distribution of the sample mean?","choices":[{"correct":true,"text":"Same center, smaller spread","feedback":"Correct! The center stays at $\\mu$, but the spread of the sample means shrinks—larger samples give more precise estimates."},{"correct":false,"text":"The center would shift upward","feedback":"The center does not move with sample size; it is always $\\mu$ for random samples."},{"correct":false,"text":"Same center, larger spread","feedback":"Larger samples REDUCE the variability of the sample mean."}],"multi":false,"hint":"Larger samples produce sample means that hug the population mean more tightly.","explanation":""},"key":"ODGEueXRpA"},{"type":"anywidget","esm":"/textbook/build/quiz-widget-30a9c49f85f8d76895c10687ac28287f.mjs","model":{"question":"A single random sample of 9 babies has a mean birth weight of 3,400 grams, not 3,500. Does this contradict the claim that the sampling distribution is centered at 3,500?","choices":[{"correct":true,"text":"No—individual sample means vary around 3,500 due to sampling variability","feedback":"Correct! Sampling variability means individual sample means differ from $\\mu$; \"centered at 3,500\" describes the average over many repeated samples."},{"correct":false,"text":"Yes—the sample mean should equal 3,500 every time","feedback":"One sample below the mean is entirely expected—about half of all sample means fall below $\\mu$."}],"multi":false,"hint":"Individual sample means vary; the center describes the long-run average of many sample means.","explanation":""},"key":"EJ6ZYCJT54"}],"key":"of4v1UECHN"}],"key":"GBVy6KVFj3"},"references":{"cite":{"order":[],"data":{}}},"footer":{"navigation":{"prev":{"title":"Finding Probabilities for a Sample Proportion","url":"/pages/p168-m12-behavior-of-sample-proportion-3-of-3","